# Branching & change discipline

## Environments (promotion path)

| Branch | Role |
| ------ | ---- |
| `dev` | Integration — **default base** for feature work |
| `staging` | QA / UAT |
| `main` | Production — Release Please target |

Full lifecycle (rebase, ticket ladder, Release Please, edge cases, skill map): [`../references/ship/release-lifecycle.md`](../references/ship/release-lifecycle.md).

**Hard rules:** rebase onto `origin/dev` before PR · GitHub **Rebase and Merge** into `dev` · never skip envs · never cherry-pick for promotion · never fix QA on `staging` (bug ticket → feature → `dev`).

Release Please = **release automation on `main`**, not a branching strategy — needs linear history + Conventional Commits from `/build` / `ship-execute`.

---

## Prefix semantics (example scheme — rename to fit your org)

| Prefix | Use when |
| --- | ----- |
| `story/` or `feature/` | Product source change (feature, refactor) |
| `bug/` | Defect fix in source |
| `hotfix/` | Production fix branched from `main` (merge back → staging → `dev`) |
| `devops/` | CI, infra, deployment scripts only |
| `task/` | Docs-only; no runtime code |

Pattern: `<prefix>/<TICKET-ID>[-short-description]`
Examples: `feature/SP-123-add-payment`, `story/SP-123-add-payment`, `bug/SP-456-login-timeout`, `hotfix/SP-999-null-guard`.

Branch from **`dev`** (hotfixes from **`main`**). Target the next env on the promotion path — not another feature branch.

**Stacked PRs:** when a change is multi-concern or exceeds ~20–30 files, land as a stack (`gh stack`) instead of one mega-PR targeting `dev`. Mid-stack PRs may target the branch below; only the bottom targets `dev`. See [`stacking-prs.mdc`](./stacking-prs.mdc) · [`skills/stacking-prs/SKILL.md`](../skills/stacking-prs/SKILL.md).

---

## PR title vs commit message

- **Commit** — Conventional Commits (Release Please parses these); subject ≤50 chars when possible
- **PR title** — carries ticket ID for automation (`SP-123 Summary` / `TICKET-123 Summary`)

---

## Author checklist (before review)

- [ ] Rebased onto current `origin/dev` (or `main` for hotfix)
- [ ] Standards + architecture respected
- [ ] Build contract tasks marked done only with evidence
- [ ] Tests at appropriate level
- [ ] Lint/format on **touched files only**
- [ ] Risk + rollback stated
- [ ] Deviations declared with plan to repay

